const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先决定一篇文档是什么",en:"Choose the document unit before the model"},body:{zh:"一篇新闻、一天的新闻集合和一家公司一年的发言，可以成为不同的文档单位。作者强调单位应服务于研究对象；聚合方式改变可保留的依赖关系，也改变统计样本数，不能仅为了文件方便而随意切分。",en:"An article, a day's news or a speaker-year can each define a document unit. Aggregation should match the research attribute. It changes both the dependence retained and the number of observations, so file convenience alone is not a sufficient reason for choosing it."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §2.1",en:"2019 journal article · §2.1"}}},{title:{zh:"清洗不是无损操作",en:"Cleaning is not information-free"},body:{zh:"删去数字、标点、常见词和罕见词，可以降低维度，却也可能删掉事件日期、否定含义或领域专有信息。作者举例说明别人眼中的停用词可能正是研究对象。应保留原文，并记录每一步过滤规则及其版本。",en:"Removing numbers, punctuation, common words and rare terms reduces dimensionality but may remove dates or domain-specific meaning. The survey stresses that one study's stop words may be another's object of interest. Preserve raw text and version each filtering decision."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §2.2",en:"2019 journal article · §2.2"}}},{title:{zh:"词频与文档频率不是同一件事",en:"Term counts differ from document prevalence"},body:{zh:"词在某篇文章出现多少次，与它出现在多少篇文章中，是两个维度。TF-IDF同时利用局部词频和语料中的文档频率；因此更换语料集合，即使单篇文本不变，其权重也可能改变。权重不是词语经济重要性的直接度量。",en:"A word's count within a document differs from the number of documents containing it. TF-IDF combines local frequency with corpus-wide prevalence. Changing the corpus may change weights even for unchanged text; a weight is not a direct measure of economic importance."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §2.2",en:"2019 journal article · §2.2"}}},{title:{zh:"词袋丢掉顺序，词组保留局部依赖",en:"Bags of words lose order; phrases retain local context"},body:{zh:"词袋只统计词语次数，不保存完整语序；二元或三元词组能保留部分相邻关系，但特征空间会快速增长。选择更长词组不自动带来更好的经济解释，应比较新增信息、稀疏程度和计算代价，而非只追求表示更复杂。",en:"Bag-of-words counts ignore order. Bigrams and trigrams retain some adjacent relationships at the cost of rapidly increasing dimensionality. Longer phrases do not automatically improve interpretation; assess the extra information, sparsity and computational cost."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §2.3",en:"2019 journal article · §2.3"}}},{title:{zh:"搜索命中数不等于拿到了语料",en:"Search counts are not access to the corpus"},body:{zh:"如果只能通过检索界面获取命中文章数，就未必能枚举全部词汇、计算文档频率或重新切分文章。作者区分这种访问方式与直接持有原始文本。保存查询条件很重要，但不能因此声称已重建完整语料。",en:"A search interface may return match counts without allowing vocabulary enumeration, document-frequency calculation or new document boundaries. The authors distinguish this from raw-text access. Preserving queries is useful but does not establish reconstruction of the corpus."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §2.5",en:"2019 journal article · §2.5"}}},{title:{zh:"词典分数与训练得到的模型分开",en:"Distinguish dictionary rules from fitted models"},body:{zh:"预先指定词典和计数规则，可以把文本变成分数，但这个步骤本身未必包含统计估计。编辑建议保留词典版本、文本版本及发布时间，再讨论分数是否对应目标概念。文档版本教程帮助保存这些材料，不替代词典有效性检验。",en:"A predefined dictionary and counting rule can produce scores without fitting a statistical model. Editorial application: retain dictionary and text versions with publication times before asking whether the score measures the intended concept. The document-ledger tutorial preserves materials, not dictionary validity."},reference:{url:"https://web.stanford.edu/~gentzkow/research/text-as-data.pdf",label:{zh:"2019年期刊版 · §3 · pp. 540–541",en:"2019 journal article · §3 · pp. 540–541"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这是2019年的方法综述。文本表示会损失信息，词典和清洗规则依赖语境；文中的英文例子不能直接成为中文金融文本的有效性证明。",en:"This is a 2019 methods survey. Text representations discard information, and dictionaries and preprocessing depend on context. English examples do not validate a Chinese financial-text implementation."}};export{e as default};
